request.description:
A deliberately invalid body — `duration: 0` is outside the documented 1–300 seconds. Expected response:

```json
{
  "error": "validation_failed",
  "issues": [
    { "path": "duration", "message": "…" }
  ]
}
```

Every 400 from the API uses this envelope: a stable `error` code plus per-field `issues`. Swap the body for `{ "duration": "abc" }`, `{}`, or invalid JSON to see the same shape with different issues.

Live task updates over WebSocket. HTTP runners cannot execute this — open the request, press **Connect**, then paste a frame below into the message bar and Send. `{{taskId}}` resolves inside the message box (it is set by **Create task**).

**1 · Subscribe** (send exactly one per socket):

```
{"type":"subscribe","taskId":"{{taskId}}"}
```

**2 · Expected sequence** — one sync frame, many progress frames, exactly one terminal frame, then silence:

```
{"type":"state","taskId":"…","status":"pending","progress":0}
{"type":"progress","taskId":"…","progress":1}
{"type":"progress","taskId":"…","progress":2}
…
{"type":"completed","taskId":"…"}
```

The `state` frame is the database-authoritative snapshot — whatever you missed while disconnected is already reflected in it.

**3 · Failure path** — create the failing task (saved as `{{failingTaskId}}`) and subscribe with:

```
{"type":"subscribe","taskId":"{{failingTaskId}}"}
```

…same sequence, terminal frame is `{"type":"failed","taskId":"…"}`.

**4 · Error frames** — malformed input is answered as a value; the socket stays open:

```
{"type":"subscribe","taskId":"not-a-uuid"}   ->  {"type":"error","error":"validation_failed","issues":[{"path":"taskId","message":"…"}]}
{"type":"subscribe","taskId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000"}  ->  {"type":"error","error":"not_found"}
send the plain text  not json                   ->  {"type":"error","error":"validation_failed","issues":[{"path":"","message":"invalid JSON"}]}
```

**5 · Recovery drill** — subscribe, close the socket mid-task, reconnect, subscribe again: the fresh `state` frame carries the current progress, so a client can never be stuck on a stale state. Processing itself never depended on the socket being open.

All frame schemas (`SubscribeMessage`, `TaskUpdate`, `ProtocolError`) are also registered in the OpenAPI document at {{baseUrl}}/docs.
